The weight the namespace carries when the node is cpu-bound, against the other
namespaces and the objects outside them.

It arbitrates rather than caps: a namespace holding a small share still takes
every idle cpu it asks for.

Setting this keyword to `default` puts the capping back where a node that
never capped anything leaves it. Removing the keyword does not: what was
written stays written, whether om wrote it or something else did.
